    "q-218773": {
      "dom_id": "step-q218773",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "By completing the square, the equation $3{x}^{2}+12x+8=0$ is equivalent to\n\n$\\,\\,3(x\\,\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+12x+8 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+12x & =-8 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4x) & =-8 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{(2)}^{2}-{(2)}^{2}] & -8 \\\\ 3[{(x+2)}^{2}-4] & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(x+2)}^{2}-3\\cdot 4 & =-8 \\\\ 3{(x+2)}^{2}-12 & =-8 \\\\ 3{(x+2)}^{2} & =-8+12 \\\\ 3{(x+2)}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
